;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; *TELESOFT (and service &12 with Y=6): SELECT THE TELESOFT FILING SYSTEM
;   - remember the current filing system number and tell it (FSCV A=6) that it is being
;     replaced
;   - point FILEV..FSCV at the extended vector entries and fill those with this ROM's
;     handlers (table at &9E15)
;   - issue service &0F (vectors changed)
;   - if TFS's state was stashed: issue service &0A so the current owner saves its own
;     state, then restore TFS's 1K from the adapter RAM and 2K from private workspace,
;     clear the adapter RAM, and restart all captures
;   - switch capture and interrupts on
; NOTE: the restore writes 3K from &0E8E, i.e. up to &1A8D, so 142 bytes at &1A00-&1A8D
; (normally the start of user memory) are overwritten with what was there when the state
; was stashed. This looks like a bug; it has not been tested.
