;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; OSFILE A=&FF: LOAD A TELESOFTWARE FILE (X/Y = OSFILE parameter block)
;   - copy the file name into page 1 (&0100) so that it is safe from being overwritten
;   - open the named file on the current page (LAC94: find its first block, apply the
;     load address from the parameter block if one was given)
;   - read decoded bytes from channel 14 and store them, through the Tube if necessary,
;     at the load address; a new block may change the address (<DLA>/<DLR>)
;   - finally write the length into the parameter block
; run_flag is set when the file is to be run (*RUN, */): "Cannot execute" is given if
; the parameter block asked for its own load address in that case.
;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.L9F4C
