;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Wait up to 60 fields for a fresh service data packet (tsdp+9, the time offset byte, is
; cleared first and reappears when a new packet arrives). Then:
;   - UTC (tsdp+13..15) is sent as BCD with every digit increased by 1: subtract &11
;   - check the hours are 00-23, else "reception error" (&FF in time_buf+11)
;   - apply the local time offset (tsdp+9): bit 6 sign, then hours and a half-hour bit
;   - note a day carry in time_buf+11 for *DATE, and format HH MM SS as ASCII
; time_buf+11 = &F0 if no packet arrived.
;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.read_time
    A3B5  08        PHP
    A3B6  A2 09     LDX #&09
    A3B8  A9 00     LDA #&00
    A3BA  9D 5C 0E  STA tsdp,X
