;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; CONVERT THE MODIFIED JULIAN DATE TO A CALENDAR DATE
; The MJD (tsdp+10..12, five BCD digits each sent +1) counts days. The routine works in
; decimal mode throughout:
;   - subtract MJD 44969, so that 1 January 1982 (MJD 44970) is day 1; 44968 or 44970
;     is used instead when the local time offset moved the date by a day (see read_time)
;   - subtract whole years (365, or 366 when the binary year in &0E35 is divisible by 4)
;     counting the BCD year up from 1982
;   - then subtract whole months using the days-per-month table at &A6E3 (February gets
;     an extra day in a leap year); what is left is the day of the month
